  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Holders page buttons **Import…** and **Export…** are enabled. Each has a hover text that says what it does.\n\n- **Export…** writes the user holders of the document to a holder file (`.camcomponents`). The file uses the component library format (`component_library::to_text`, `camcraft-components/1`). A user holder is a holder row of the component table whose id is not `builtin:`. A holder is an adaptive item with a spindle taper on its machine side, the same set that the Holders page lists.\n- **Import…** reads such a file and adds each holder as a user holder, without a library link, in one undo step. The new undoable command is `ImportHolders` (`crates/app/src/commands/holder_file.rs`). A row keeps its file id when the id is free. An id that the document, the component library or an earlier row holds gets a new `user:holder:<name>` id, then ` (2)`, ` (3)`, as \"Copy as user holder\" does.\n- A file that is not correct is refused by name, and the document does not change. This includes bad JSON, a truncated file, a wrong envelope, a file with no row, a row that is not a holder, and a holder outline that is not correct (a negative radius, fewer than 3 points). The refusal shows on the Tool pane.\n- MCP: the new tools `export_holders` and `import_holders` (`crates/app/src/mcp/holder_file_tools.rs`) use the same function and the same command. `export_holders` asks for file-write approval in a live session (`mcp/live.rs`). `import_holders` refuses by name when the component library cannot be read, because then it cannot keep the new ids clear of the library ids. It does not use the built-in ids only. The generated reference `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the guide row in `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md` name the two tools.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/4389-holder-files.md` (the format, the id rule, the refusals).\n\n`tool_library_dialog/mod.rs` is not changed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (main): the two buttons are disabled, and the hover names #4389.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4463/before.png)\n\nAfter: the two buttons are enabled, and the hover says what Import does.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4463/after.png)\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-app` `tool_library_holders` (`holder_files.rs`):\n  - `an_export_imports_into_a_new_document_byte_stable_in_one_undo_step`\n  - `a_held_id_takes_a_new_user_holder_id`\n  - `a_file_that_is_not_correct_is_refused_by_name_with_nothing_applied` (the degenerate input test: bad JSON, truncated, wrong format, binary, not a holder, no row, an outline with a negative radius, an outline with fewer than 3 points)\n  - `a_document_with_no_user_holder_is_refused_and_a_builtin_row_is_not_exported`\n  - `mcp_export_and_import_holders_use_the_one_command` (also: an unreadable component library refuses the import, and nothing is applied)\n- `camcraft-ui` lib (`egui_app::tests::tool_library_holder_files`):\n  - `import_and_export_stand_enabled_with_a_hover_text`\n  - `export_then_import_adds_user_holders_in_one_undo_step`\n  - `a_file_that_is_not_correct_is_refused_on_the_tool_pane`\n\n## Gate\n\nHead `933e1774d`. One `lanes` run (`--needs app --pool`, Mac lane). Log: `gate-4463-933e1774d.log`, first line `head 933e1774d0f430f683c7e7e6f99ba5fdf796e4da`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 394 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `app suites: tool_library_holders`, `app suites: mcp_doc_drift` and `ui suites: lib`. The step `site tests` is SKIPPED (zola is not installed on the lane). This is not a pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 4 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (`light build`, `motion light: lib`, `motion light: adaptive2d`, `app light: pocket_pass_start`).\n- `camcraft-ui` `#[test]` count: 2019 at the merge base, 2022 at the head. This change adds no UI test.\n- No post and no toolpath changed, so the example catalog suites do not apply.\n\nEarlier head `5b0ad957e` (two merges of `origin/main`): the hand edits keep both sides where #4391 added `holder_shape_tools` / `edit_user_holder` next to the new holder file tools: `mcp/mod.rs`, `mcp/component_tools.rs`, `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (tool count 140) and the guide row.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The native file dialogs. The tests call `export_holders_to` and `import_holders_from` directly.\n- The browser build. It refuses the two buttons with the existing `browser_files` texts, as on the Tools page.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill gets no row for the two tools. A skill edit is a process change, so this PR does not make it. The generated reference and the guide name the tools.\n\nChangelog: The Holders page imports and exports holder files: Export writes the document's user holders to a `.camcomponents` file, and Import adds the holders of such a file as user holders in one undo step (MCP: `export_holders`, `import_holders`).\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4389\n",
